{
  "id": "uncertainty-principle",
  "term": "uncertainty principle",
  "definition": "The uncertainty principle here refers to a basic limit on how precisely information in a signal can be resolved at the same time in both the time domain and the frequency domain. In learning-related time-series analysis, it means methods must balance detail about when changes happen with detail about their rhythmic or frequency pattern.",
